+          "quote": "Let $X$ be a real or complex Banach space and let $A\\in\\mathcal B(X)$ ([[def-bounded-linear-operator]]). For $t\\in\\mathbb R$ define $E(t):=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty\\frac{t^n}{n!}A^n$. Then the series converges absolutely in the operator norm $\\|\\cdot\\|$ of $\\mathcal B(X)$, uniformly for $t$ in compact subsets of $\\mathbb R$; $E(t)\\in\\mathcal B(X)$ with $\\|E(t)\\| \\le e^{|t|\\|A\\|}$; $E(0)=I$ and $E(t+s)=E(t)E(s)$ for all $s,t\\in\\mathbb R$; $t\\mapsto E(t)$ is of class $C^\\infty$ in the operator norm with $$E'(t)=AE(t)=E(t)A,$$ and $\\|E(t)-I-tA\\| \\le\\frac{t^2}{2}\\|A\\|^2e^{|t|\\|A\\|}$, so that $\\frac{E(t)-I}{t}\\to A$ in operator norm as $t\\to0$. In particular $E$ is a uniformly continuous (hence strongly continuous) group of bounded operators on $X$ whose generator is the bounded operator $A$.",
